# Windows launchers and the plain-text instructions MUST keep CRLF line
# endings. A .bat file with Unix line endings can fail on Windows in ways
# that are very hard to diagnose - "goto" and multi-line blocks are the
# ones that bite - and it looks like a broken laptop rather than a broken
# file. Notepad on older builds also runs .txt files together into one
# line without them.
#
# Git normalises line endings on checkout unless it is told not to, so
# this file is what stops a kit that works turning into a kit that
# doesn't, purely by being cloned on a different machine.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.txt text eol=crlf

# These are fine either way and Python/browsers don't care.
*.py text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary - never touch these.
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.eml binary
